# The repo tracks what the deployed dashboard needs, plus what the weekly
# refresh Action needs to keep it current. Everything else - the training and
# analysis pipeline, the frozen release, tests, docs - stays local. Nothing here
# is deleted, only untracked.
#
# NOTE the `dir/*` patterns below. Git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so `reports/` would make every `!reports/keep.json` negation below
# silently do nothing. This already bit once.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
graphify-out/
.vscode/
_fix_code.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local only
frozen/
REPORT.md
CONTEXT.md
CLAUDE.md
pyrightconfig.json

# tests/, docs/ and experiments/ used to sit in the list above. They are tracked
# now, for a reason that showed up in practice: nothing guarded the artifacts the
# dashboard serves. The weekly refresh regenerates and commits the model bundles
# every Tuesday, and with the suite untracked CI could not run a single check
# against them - the first sign of a bad artifact would have been a broken
# dashboard. docs/adr carries the reasoning behind the model decisions, and the
# ADRs cite experiments/ by path as their evidence, so all three travel together
# or none of them are much use.

# The pipeline that produced the models. Rebuilding any of it needs the 565 MB
# Brazil parquet, which is not in the repo either.
train_model1.py
train_model2.py
train_lstm.py
finalize_model1.py
finalize_peds.py
transfer_srilanka.py
transfer_test.py
run_audit.py
run_ablation.py
shap_model2.py
spatial_and_ablation.py
robustness_model2.py
calibration_and_errors.py
leakage_audit.py
verify_fixes.py
freeze_v2.py
fetch_full.py
derive_reports.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data
# Raw datasets are downloaded by the pipeline. The two Sri Lanka inputs travel
# with the repo because the weekly refresh needs them on a clean checkout.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/srilanka_weekly_district.csv
!data/raw/srilanka_weather_daily.parquet
# 20 KB of monthly ENSO index. Shipped for the same reason as the two above: the
# weekly CI refresh has to build a panel on a clean checkout, and it must not fail
# because NOAA is unreachable that morning.
!data/raw/enso_nino34.csv

data/processed/*
!data/processed/srilanka_history.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- models
# Only the four the app loads. model2_outbreak is the Brazil model, which the
# app never opens, and the LSTM is training-only.
models/*
!models/model1_screening.joblib
!models/peds_complications.joblib
!models/srilanka_outbreak.joblib
!models/srilanka_emergence.joblib

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reports
# The artifacts the app reads, plus the ones the refresh rewrites. The CI job
# runs `git add -A reports/`, so anything not negated here would be re-added on
# the next Tuesday run.
reports/*
!reports/cbc_population_medians.json
!reports/data_freshness.json
!reports/dataset_audit.csv
!reports/leakage_audit.json
!reports/model1_operating_points.json
!reports/model2_calibration_errors.json
!reports/model2_headtohead.csv
!reports/model2_information_ablation.csv
!reports/model2_robustness.json
!reports/model2_spatial_holdout.csv
!reports/model2_summary.json
!reports/peds_final.json
!reports/reporting_delay_stress.csv
!reports/situation_freshness.json
!reports/srilanka_current_risk.csv
!reports/srilanka_continuation.json
!reports/srilanka_dual_risk.csv
!reports/srilanka_emergence.json
!reports/srilanka_feature_importance.csv
!reports/srilanka_latest_situation.csv
!reports/srilanka_situation_history.csv
!reports/srilanka_transfer.csv
requirements-dev.txt
